### WEBSOCKET /v1/ws — push notifications channel
###
### When to use: to receive matchmaking events pushed by the server (no polling):
### pairing, match pending confirmation, match confirmed/cancelled, PONG.
###
### How to use (IntelliJ IDEA HTTP Client):
###   1. Start auth-service + matchmaking-api + matchmaking-engine (engine does the pairing).
###   2. Run auth-service/POST-v1-auth-login.http first — it captures {{token}}.
###   3. Run the request line below ("Open in WebSocket" / run gutter icon). The session
###      stays open; run each ### message section to send a frame. Watch the Response panel
###      for PONG and the engine's MATCH_PENDING_CONFIRMATION / MATCH_CONFIRMED frames.
###
### NOTE: this file is IntelliJ-specific. VS Code's REST Client does not support
### WebSocket — use the Python/websocat snippet in this folder's README there.

WEBSOCKET ws://localhost:8080/v1/ws?token={{token}}

### Send PING — expect a PONG frame back
{"type":"PING","payload":{}}

### Invalid JSON — expect an ERROR frame (run this to validate error handling)
not-json

### Unknown type — expect an ERROR frame
{"type":"WAT","payload":{}}

### Confirm a match (use matchId from the MATCH_PENDING_CONFIRMATION frame)
{"type":"MATCH_CONFIRM","payload":{"matchId":"match-xxxx"}}

### Decline a match (dissolves the group; both players go back to the queue)
{"type":"MATCH_DECLINE","payload":{"matchId":"match-xxxx"}}
